{"id": "who-gets-a-yes", "title": "Who gets a yes: area gaps mostly vanish like for like; the power to object follows income", "seconds": 158.6, "voice": "elevenlabs:iPYqcpY8j8Ap4jUf28I3", "narrator": "Michael", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-25", "key": "7d21853563438574", "words": 385, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "sfmap", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "story[0]"], "text": "A San Francisco neighbor can force a hearing on a home project that meets the code.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.54, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "sfmap", "hood": "Marina", "hoodLabel": "Marina", "zoom": "hood", "scale": 2.6, "kicker": "Review requests"}, "wt": [0.12, 0.17, 0.32, 0.84, 1.27, 1.51, 1.77, 1.86, 2.31, 2.47, 2.56, 2.73, 3.24, 3.46, 3.75, 3.88]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "sfmap", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "story[0]"], "text": "It’s called a review request.", "t0": 4.66, "t1": 6.5, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "sfmap", "hood": "Marina", "hoodLabel": "Marina", "zoom": "hood", "scale": 2.6, "kicker": "Review requests"}, "emph": ["review request"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.58, 0.73, 1.15]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "sfmap", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "In the Marina, how many per 1,000 home permits?", "t0": 6.62, "t1": 9.5, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "sfmap", "hood": "Marina", "hoodLabel": "Marina", "zoom": "hood", "scale": 2.6, "kicker": "Review requests per 1,000 residential permits", "zoomOn": "marina"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.04, 0.14, 0.86, 1.0, 1.21, 1.39, 1.54, 1.93, 2.16]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "story[3]"], "text": "115.", "t0": 9.5, "t1": 11.2, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "115", "label": "review requests per 1,000 full residential permits, Marina", "sub": "the city: 46"}, "emph": ["115"], "wt": [0.04, 0.77, 1.07]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 11.72, "t1": 13.66, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.18, 0.3, 1.04, 1.18, 1.28]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "sfmap", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Across town, in the Western Addition? Just 9.", "t0": 13.78, "t1": 16.9, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "sfmap", "hood": "Western Addition", "hoodLabel": "Western Addition", "zoom": "hood", "scale": 2.6, "kicker": "Review requests per 1,000 residential permits"}, "emph": ["9"], "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.72, 0.78, 0.87, 1.21, 1.81, 2.64]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "suspicious[4].what"], "text": "In thirds, by income: the top third files 74 per 1,000 permits.", "t0": 17.12, "t1": 22.53, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["highest-income third", "74 per 1,000"], "b": ["lowest-income third", "21 per 1,000"], "kicker": "Review requests, neighborhoods in thirds"}, "emph": ["74"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.79, 0.94, 1.76, 1.89, 2.19, 2.48, 2.89, 3.84, 4.19, 4.38, 4.74]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "suspicious[4].what"], "text": "The bottom, 21.", "t0": 22.65, "t1": 24.35, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["highest-income third", "74 per 1,000"], "b": ["lowest-income third", "21 per 1,000"], "kicker": "Review requests, neighborhoods in thirds"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 1.0]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "By race: 71 where white residents are most, 20 where fewest.", "t0": 24.47, "t1": 29.48, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["most white residents", "71 per 1,000"], "b": ["fewest white residents", "20 per 1,000"], "kicker": "Review requests, neighborhoods in thirds"}, "emph": ["20"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.62, 1.5, 1.72, 2.04, 2.43, 2.61, 3.13, 4.01, 4.46]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "That’s who is able to slow a project down.", "t0": 29.6, "t1": 32.12, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["most white residents", "71 per 1,000"], "b": ["fewest white residents", "20 per 1,000"], "kicker": "Review requests, neighborhoods in thirds"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.45, 0.69, 0.82, 1.03, 1.18, 1.48, 1.58, 2.12]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "Since 2022, review was taken in 38 of 93 decided requests.", "t0": 32.24, "t1": 37.53, "shot": "b6b", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["review taken, 2022 to 2026", "38 of 93"], "b": ["permits refused", "0"]}, "emph": ["38 of 93"], "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.47, 1.47, 1.79, 1.95, 2.27, 2.4, 3.18, 3.4, 3.89, 4.43]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "No permit was refused.", "t0": 37.65, "t1": 39.08, "shot": "b6b", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["review taken, 2022 to 2026", "38 of 93"], "b": ["permits refused", "0"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.56, 0.88]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "story[1]"], "text": "Now outcomes.", "t0": 39.3, "t1": 40.7, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "5,392 applications", "kicker": "The outcomes", "sub": "special planning approvals decided since 2015"}, "wt": [0.17, 0.33]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "story[1]"], "text": "Of 5,392 special planning applications since 2015,", "t0": 40.82, "t1": 46.33, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "5,392 applications", "kicker": "The outcomes", "sub": "special planning approvals decided since 2015"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.5, 0.97, 1.29, 1.64, 2.23, 2.62, 3.03, 3.68, 3.89, 4.16]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "story[1]"], "text": "how many weren’t approved?", "t0": 46.33, "t1": 48.19, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "5,392 applications", "kicker": "The outcomes", "sub": "special planning approvals decided since 2015"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.18, 0.38, 0.88]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["oneLine", "amount"], "text": "26.9 percent.", "t0": 48.19, "t1": 50.84, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "26.9%", "label": "not approved, citywide", "sub": "only 104 refused outright; most withdrawn or cancelled"}, "emph": ["26.9"], "wt": [0.04, 1.4, 1.72, 1.95]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "slam", "ref": ["story[1]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Only 104 were refused. Most were withdrawn, and applicants withdraw for their own reasons.", "t0": 51.36, "t1": 57.57, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "slam", "words": ["104", "refused"], "sub": "the rest withdrawn or cancelled"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.43, 0.75, 1.15, 1.53, 2.29, 2.97, 3.19, 4.03, 4.18, 4.65, 5.03, 5.17, 5.38, 5.59]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "sfmap", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "story[3]"], "text": "Compare like with like, giving every neighborhood the same mix of projects.", "t0": 57.69, "t1": 61.84, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "sfmap", "hood": "Outer Mission", "hoodLabel": "Outer Mission", "zoom": "hood", "scale": 2.6, "kicker": "Like for like"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.39, 0.69, 0.93, 1.56, 1.83, 2.09, 2.55, 2.72, 3.05, 3.32, 3.51]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "sfmap", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "story[3]"], "text": "One stands out beyond chance: Outer Mission.", "t0": 61.96, "t1": 64.69, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "sfmap", "hood": "Outer Mission", "hoodLabel": "Outer Mission", "zoom": "hood", "scale": 2.6, "kicker": "Like for like"}, "emph": ["Outer Mission"], "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.65, 0.95, 1.3, 1.94, 2.25]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "31 of 59 not approved, where 19 were expected.", "t0": 64.81, "t1": 69.24, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Outer Mission, not approved", "31 of 59"], "b": ["expected for its mix", "19"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.58, 0.8, 1.51, 1.81, 2.4, 3.02, 3.61, 3.88]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "And one district, District 11: 70 against 52.", "t0": 69.36, "t1": 74.03, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Outer Mission, not approved", "31 of 59"], "b": ["expected for its mix", "19"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.39, 1.24, 1.6, 2.74, 3.33, 3.86]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "Like for like, projects also fail less where incomes are higher.", "t0": 74.15, "t1": 77.9, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Like for like", "sub": "non-approval lower where incomes are higher: -0.52"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.42, 0.94, 1.43, 1.8, 2.1, 2.46, 2.74, 3.18, 3.33]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "story[6]"], "text": "Professionals do a little better.", "t0": 78.12, "t1": 80.11, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Not approved, against expected for the same kinds of case", "rows": [["registered permit consultant", "22.9% (27.3%)"], ["lobbied projects", "24.2% (26.6%)"], ["firms whose staff gave to campaigns", "24.4% (27.7%)"], ["no firm named", "28.0% (26.7%)"]]}, "wt": [0.65, 0.9, 1.11, 1.18, 1.47]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "story[6]"], "text": "With a registered permit consultant,", "t0": 80.23, "t1": 82.37, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Not approved, against expected for the same kinds of case", "rows": [["registered permit consultant", "22.9% (27.3%)"], ["lobbied projects", "24.2% (26.6%)"], ["firms whose staff gave to campaigns", "24.4% (27.7%)"], ["no firm named", "28.0% (26.7%)"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.24, 0.72, 1.12]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "story[6]"], "text": "22.9 percent not approved, against 27.3 expected.", "t0": 82.37, "t1": 88.13, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Not approved, against expected for the same kinds of case", "rows": [["registered permit consultant", "22.9% (27.3%)"], ["lobbied projects", "24.2% (26.6%)"], ["firms whose staff gave to campaigns", "24.4% (27.7%)"], ["no firm named", "28.0% (26.7%)"]]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.47, 0.89, 1.07, 1.68, 1.98, 2.58, 3.5, 4.05, 4.4, 4.88]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why"], "text": "So do firms whose staff gave to campaigns. Better paperwork, or access? The records can’t tell.", "t0": 88.25, "t1": 94.16, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "better-prepared applications and access"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.35, 0.78, 1.01, 1.38, 1.59, 1.74, 2.58, 2.87, 3.63, 3.92, 4.6, 4.78, 5.22, 5.56]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].where", "notEstablished[5]"], "text": "Firms are matched by name alone: the records do not show whether they are the same organization.", "t0": 94.28, "t1": 99.41, "shot": "b14n", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "they are matched by name alone"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.44, 0.82, 1.08, 1.48, 2.37, 2.51, 2.84, 2.97, 3.12, 3.37, 3.61, 3.7, 3.85, 4.05, 4.33]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[2]", "story[12]"], "text": "At the commissions since 2022, lobbied projects were changed more often, not less:", "t0": 99.53, "t1": 105.6, "shot": "b14b", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["lobbied before the vote", "23.5%"], "b": ["the rest", "13.9%"]}, "emph": ["more often, not less"], "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.19, 0.79, 1.11, 1.37, 2.37, 2.78, 3.18, 3.39, 3.78, 4.0, 4.74, 5.02]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[2]", "story[12]"], "text": "23.5 percent against 13.9.", "t0": 105.6, "t1": 108.88, "shot": "b14bx", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["lobbied before the vote", "23.5%"], "b": ["the rest", "13.9%"]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.46, 0.78, 1.02, 1.66, 2.11, 2.47, 2.86]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "And where are new homes even proposed?", "t0": 109.1, "t1": 111.18, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["District 6", "418 homes per 1,000 residents"], "b": ["District 1", "21"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.33, 0.51, 0.68, 1.07, 1.35]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "District 6: 418 per 1,000 residents.", "t0": 111.18, "t1": 116.0, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["District 6", "418 homes per 1,000 residents"], "b": ["District 1", "21"]}, "wt": [0.04, 1.05, 1.96, 2.37, 2.71, 3.25, 3.65, 3.84, 4.24]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "District 1: 21.", "t0": 116.0, "t1": 119.06, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["District 6", "418 homes per 1,000 residents"], "b": ["District 1", "21"]}, "wt": [0.04, 1.15, 2.35]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why"], "text": "Most districts aren’t saying no at hearings. Projects aren’t filed there. Zoning decides first.", "t0": 119.18, "t1": 123.83, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Zoning decides first", "sub": "62.7% of proposed homes in District 6, District 5 and District 9"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.53, 0.69, 0.98, 1.16, 1.3, 1.92, 2.37, 2.71, 2.91, 3.32, 3.81, 4.23]}, {"scene": "sponsors", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "Project sponsors were identified in 216 of 251 Board appeal files.", "t0": 124.05, "t1": 130.57, "shot": "sponsor-count", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "akdeniz", "text": "Signed sponsor response", "mark": "Signed sponsor response", "kicker": "San Francisco Board of Supervisors"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.41, 1.03, 1.18, 1.73, 1.9, 2.04, 2.41, 3.16, 3.63, 3.77, 4.07, 4.84, 5.45, 5.83]}, {"scene": "sponsors", "kind": "record", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "The sponsor backs the project. The appellant challenges a decision about it.", "t0": 130.69, "t1": 135.09, "shot": "sponsor-roles", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "relationship", "context": "Board appeals", "heading": "Who is identified in the file?", "source": "slowstreets", "rows": [{"icon": "file", "label": "Project sponsor", "value": "SFMTA on the first Slow Streets phase"}, {"icon": "gap", "label": "Sponsor still unidentified", "value": "Thirty-five files"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.7, 0.94, 1.06, 1.82, 2.37, 2.84, 3.42, 3.5, 3.9, 4.16]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[4]"], "text": "None of this shows bias by any commissioner, supervisor or planner.", "t0": 135.31, "t1": 139.25, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Bias by any commissioner, supervisor or planner", "That outcomes follow income at the finer level of Census tracts"]}, "wt": [0.06, 0.12, 0.25, 0.45, 0.78, 1.28, 1.46, 1.65, 2.4, 3.08, 3.28]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[4]"], "text": "And by Census tract, the income link is within chance.", "t0": 139.37, "t1": 142.56, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Bias by any commissioner, supervisor or planner", "That outcomes follow income at the finer level of Census tracts"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.29, 0.76, 1.44, 1.55, 1.93, 2.13, 2.26, 2.57]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]"], "text": "What would settle it? Hearing minutes for Outer Mission and District 11.", "t0": 142.68, "t1": 146.44, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Hearing minutes for Outer Mission and District 11"}, {"who": "", "what": "Who files review requests: the published field is blank"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.06, 0.27, 0.54, 0.81, 1.67, 2.01, 2.21, 2.47, 2.8, 2.94, 3.34]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[1]"], "text": "And who files review requests: that field is mostly blank.", "t0": 146.56, "t1": 150.47, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Hearing minutes for Outer Mission and District 11"}, {"who": "", "what": "Who files review requests: the published field is blank"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.32, 0.76, 1.17, 1.97, 2.25, 2.67, 2.9, 3.32]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "This compares areas. It’s not a finding about any decision-maker or applicant.", "t0": 150.59, "t1": 155.08, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.74, 1.41, 1.69, 1.81, 1.93, 2.31, 2.53, 2.73, 3.59, 3.86]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 155.2, "t1": 157.72, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.37, 0.44, 0.54, 1.23, 1.62, 1.78]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "lead1": "Lead 1 · who objects", "lead2": "Lead 2 · who gets a yes", "lead3": "Lead 3 · professionals", "lead4": "Lead 4 · where homes are proposed", "close": "Where it stands", "sponsors": "Sponsors and appellants"}, "look": "map", "hook": "contrast"}